// ParseOctal converts an octal number represented as a string into its
// decimal equivalent. The conversion is done by hand, without relying
// on any library function that would do it for us.
//
// Invalid input (a string containing any character other than the octal
// digits 0-7, or an empty string) is treated as octal 0 and an error is returned.
